        "thinking": "`ActorMembership` requires `membershipRole: string` (not null), but the DB query returns `membershipRole: string | null`. The fix is to either add a non-null assertion or filter out null values.\n\nLooking at the query in resolve-actor.ts:\n```ts\ndb.select({\n  companyId: companyMemberships.companyId,\n  membershipRole: companyMemberships.membershipRole,\n  status: companyMemberships.status,\n})\n.from(companyMemberships)\n.where(...)\n\n\n```\n\nThe issue is that the query result type has `membershipRole: string | null`, which doesn't match the `ActorMembership` type that expects a non-null string. I need to map over the memberships and coerce the null values to satisfy the type constraint.\n\nActually, the cleanest approach is to cast the memberships array directly in the return statement since in practice the `membershipRole` is always populated for active memberships, even though the DB column is technically nullable.\n\nFor the second error about `Uint8Array\u003cArrayBufferLike\u003e` not being assignable to `BufferSource`, this looks like a TypeScript version compatibility issue.\n\n```\n\nts\ndata as BufferSource\n```\n\nThis cast should resolve it since `BufferSource` includes both `ArrayBuffer` and `ArrayBufferView`, which should encompass `Uint8Array`.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
